                "id": "123-1580492962881-1580492968342-0",
                "title": "Cassiopeia A Supernova Remnant",
                "unitCode": "OCIO_DPO3D",
                "type": "edanmdm",
                "url": "edanmdm:dpo_3d_200012",
                "content": {
                    "freetext": {
                        "notes": [
                            {
                                "label": "Summary",
                                "content": "This result shows Cassiopeia A, called Cas A for short, coming alive through the third dimension of space. Utilizing a technique borrowed from medical imaging, astronomers now have a way to travel through the heart of Cas A using data from NASA's Chandra and Spitzer telescopes. The different colors shown here correspond to different chemical elements present in the debris from the supernova explosion."
                            }
                        ],
